{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1499254-how-does-the-umbra-work","id":1499254,"title":"how does the umbra work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-09T15:37:27-08:00","id":1499254,"title":"how does the umbra work?","content":"it is very confusing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-09T16:37:19-08:00","id":1499257,"title":"","content":"It's a set of three parallel worlds to an imaginary side of the physical one, separated by a barrier known as the Gauntlet, which largely keeps each world to its own devices (mages and other beings, such as werebeasts or ghosts, are capable of breaching these barriers, and they thin down to nothing at some nodes). The Low and High are more their own thing, and are respectively the Underworld of Wraith and the Astral Plane. The Middle Umbra is the closest to the physical world, and the only one that only requires Spirit to visit (Low requires Entropy, and certain regions of the High Umbra require that you leave your body behind and project there via Mind). Past a certain point, the Middle also gives way to the Deep Umbra, where a lot of alien spirits dwell. Also worth noting that if you're going through Werewolf books to find out things about the Umbra, the structure is different - Mage posits that space past the Asteroid Belt is the spirit world, whereas in Werewolf, the Aetherial Realm of the Near (Middle) Umbra continues on as a near-perfect mirror of the physical universe, vast reaches of outer space and all, though with a very low Gauntlet the further you get from Earth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T10:52:51-08:00","id":1499294,"title":"","content":"You are correct that information about the Umbra can be contradictory or confusing, and there are at least a couple of reasons for this:<br /> <br /> Saur Ops Specialist has already hit on this a bit, but part of that comes down to different game-lines, like Werewolf and Mage, depicting the Umbra slightly differently. This is because the different games have different themes, and the slightly different rules for Spirits and the Umbra are written to better suit the themes of the game for which they are being written. It's also complicated by the fact that earlier editions of World of Darkness tried to depict all of the game-lines existing in the same world, while later ones pulled back from that a bit to focus on supporting the themes and setting of their specific game and let crossover be more of an optional thing.<br /> <br /> The other fact that complicates thing is that the Umbra is contradictory or confusing on purpose at times. There are all sorts of exceptions and niche cases, and they aren't always fleshed out very thoroughly. That's at least partly to give Storytellers the freedom to use the Umbra for all sorts of weird cases and stories that might not fit into the printed rules and source material but would make for a fun game, with the added benefit that you can throw things at players that might catch them off guard if they're expecting you to stick strictly to printed source material.<br /> <br /> Addressing more specific concerns or questions would probably require more specific examples <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-10T22:43:14-08:00","id":1499349,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that you get a general view on it, and then introduce your own design to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T10:32:51-08:00","id":1499956,"title":"","content":"I would say that each of the Corebooks of M:tA are vital, key, and important in regard to understanding the Spirit World / the Umbra, and also getting a sense and being able to think up good, cool, and nice ideas in regard to the Umbra's various zones / levels / locations / regions. Reading the Corebooks definitely, carefully, and completely can also be very helpful in regard to analyzing and comprehending kinds / types of places, and particular identifable and defined areas within the Spirit World / the Umbra. <br /> <br /> The Convention Books and the Tradition Guides also tend to be of such nature and quality that each could very well be positive, meaningful, and nice in regard to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}